{"name":"Tandoori Red","hex":"#d25762","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tandoori","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked in a tandoor."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dish that was cooked in a tandoor.","A curry meal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tandoori"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tandoor","blocks":[{"text":"A tandoor is a large vase-shaped oven, usually made of clay. Since antiquity, tandoors have been used to bake unleavened flatbreads, such as roti and traditional lavash, as well as leavened ones, such as naan and tandoor bread or matnakash. It is also used to roast meat and vegetables. Tandoors are predominantly used in South Asia, Western Asia, Central Asia, and the Horn of Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Luxury_tandoor.png/330px-Luxury_tandoor.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tandoor"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG/250px-Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG/500px-Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG/250px-Charcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharcoal_Fired_S.Steel_Body_Tandoor%2C_with_ash_tray_%26_temp._meter.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg/250px-Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg/500px-Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg/250px-Coal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoal_fired_Drum_Tandoor.jpg"},{"src